Passing down arguments to multiple functions with `...` causes error from `*_scale`.
This happens under `ggplot2` versions 3.3.5, 3.3.6, and 3.3.6.9000.
```r
# plotting function
fooPlot <- function(data, varX, varY, ...) {
  p <- ggplot(data, aes_string(x = varX, y = varY, color = "Species")) +geom_point()
  return(p)
}

fooPlot(iris, "Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width")


# higher function that calls the plotting function
fooMother <- function(x, ...) {
  p <- fooPlot(x, ...)
  return(p)
}

fooMother(iris, varX = "Sepal.Length", varY = "Sepal.Width")


# another higher function that calls the plotting function
# also allows to modify legend labels
fooFather <- function(x, ...) {
  p <- fooPlot(x, ...)
  p <- p + scale_color_manual(values = c("indianred1", "springgreen2", "cornflowerblue"), ...)
  return(p)
}

fooFather(iris, varX = "Sepal.Length", varY = "Sepal.Width", labels = LETTERS[1:3])

```
It can be rectified by adding a `...` argument to `discrete_scale`.

